{#
  Is this person historical: dead on the record's own evidence, or born long
  enough ago that they cannot be living.

  The archive does not publish a family graph of living people. A relation
  between two documented historical figures is history; a living person's
  family structure is not the archive's to state. This is the test that decides
  which is which, shared by the family calculation in _layouts/base.twig, the
  Family box and the relatives' lines in it.

  It FAILS CLOSED. Undetermined is treated as living: a record with no death
  date, no casualty record, no obituary and no birth year says nothing about
  whether the person is alive, and silence is not evidence of death.

  Historical is any one of:
    - a war memorial casualty record
    - a death date on the record (deathDate, deathDateEdtf, mpDateOfDeath)
    - a live obituary for the person, either direction
    - a birth year more than 120 years ago

  Prints '1' for historical and nothing otherwise, so callers test it with
  |trim. Mirrors the guard in scripts/import/import_ruiz_census.php, which
  refuses to write a relation this would hide.
#}
{% macro historical(e) %}
  {%- set h = [] -%}
  {%- for f in (e.fieldLayout ? e.fieldLayout.customFields : []) -%}{%- set h = h|merge([f.handle]) -%}{%- endfor -%}
  {%- set yes = e.section and e.section.handle == 'warMemorials' -%}
  {%- for f in ['deathDate', 'deathDateEdtf', 'mpDateOfDeath'] -%}
    {%- if not yes and f in h and (e.getFieldValue(f) ~ '') matches '/\\d{3}/' -%}{%- set yes = true -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if not yes and 'personObituaries' in h and e.personObituaries.exists() -%}{%- set yes = true -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if not yes and craft.entries().section('obituaries').relatedTo({ targetElement: e, field: 'obitSubject' }).exists() -%}{%- set yes = true -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if not yes -%}
    {#- The first four-digit year in whichever birth field is filled. An
        uncertain year ('1847?-03-27') still counts: uncertainty of a year or
        two does not move anyone across a 120-year line. -#}
    {%- set y = '' -%}
    {%- for f in ['birthDateEdtf', 'birthDate', 'wmDateOfBirth', 'mpDateOfBirth'] -%}
      {%- set v = f in h ? (e.getFieldValue(f) ~ '')|trim : '' -%}
      {%- if not y and v matches '/\\b(1[5-9]\\d\\d|20\\d\\d)\\b/' -%}
        {%- set y = v|replace('/^.*?\\b(1[5-9]\\d\\d|20\\d\\d)\\b.*$/s', '$1') -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- if y and (y + 0) <= (now|date('Y')) - 120 -%}{%- set yes = true -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if yes %}1{% endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

{#
  The one exception to the family rule (Nathan, 29 September 2026): kinship
  between two documented public officeholders, when the relationship is itself
  public record. A father and son who served on the same council are history
  of the council, not private family structure.

  Both conditions, never one:
    1. each person holds at least one officeHolding record (holdingPerson);
    2. the holder's own footnotes cite a source that names the relationship:
       a footnote whose text names the other person and a kinship word.
  Called with the child as holder for a parent link, either way for siblings.
  Never for spouses, never for a relative without an office, never for an
  unsourced link. It takes effect only when officeHolding has records; until
  then it passes nobody.

  Prints '1' when both hold, nothing otherwise.
#}
{% macro publicKin(holder, other) %}
  {%- set office = (craft.app.entries.getSectionByHandle('officeHoldings') ?? null) is not null -%}
  {%- set a = office and craft.entries().section('officeHoldings').relatedTo({ targetElement: holder, field: 'holdingPerson' }).exists() -%}
  {%- set b = a and craft.entries().section('officeHoldings').relatedTo({ targetElement: other, field: 'holdingPerson' }).exists() -%}
  {%- set sourced = false -%}
  {%- if b and holder.fieldLayout and holder.fieldLayout.getFieldByHandle('footnotes') -%}
    {%- for r in (holder.getFieldValue('footnotes') ?? []) -%}
      {%- set t = (r.note ?? '') ~ '' -%}
      {%- if not sourced and other.title and t matches '/' ~ other.title|replace({'/': '\\/', '.': '\\.'}) ~ '/' and t matches '/\\b(son|daughter|father|mother|brother|sister|child|parent)s?\\b/i' -%}
        {%- set sourced = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if b and sourced %}1{% endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
